---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Hanfu Trip Packing List: Apps & Clothes"
  description="Packing checklist for a traditional clothing trip: essential apps like Alipay and VPN, what to wear under Hanfu and qipao, photoshoot prep, and camera gear."
  canonicalUrl="/plan-trip/packing"
  articleDate="2026-08-03"
  breadcrumbs={{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Plan Your Trip", url: "/plan-trip/" }, { name: "Packing List", url: "/plan-trip/packing/" }}>
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16"><div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#b5343a] tracking-[0.15em] uppercase">Plan Your Trip · Packing</span>
    <h1 class="font-serif-sc text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-stone-900 mt-3">What to Pack: Your Hanfu Trip Checklist</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">Packing for a traditional clothing trip is different from regular travel. You''ll be changing costumes, walking ancient sites, and taking photos all day.</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">Essential Apps (Install Before You Leave)</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-stone-900">Alipay / WeChat Pay <span class="text-xs text-red-600">— Critical</span></h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1">China is almost cashless. Set up Alipay with passport + international card before departure. Test it.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-stone-900">VPN <span class="text-xs text-red-600">— Critical</span></h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1">Google, Instagram, WhatsApp all blocked. ExpressVPN, Astrill, or LetsVPN. Install + test before departure.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-stone-900">Didi + trip.com</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1">Didi for ride-hailing (like Uber). trip.com for trains and hotels in English.</p></div>
    </div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">What to Wear Under Hanfu / Qipao</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-stone-200 text-left"><th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold">Item</th><th class="py-3 font-semibold">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Nude strapless bra</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs text-stone-500">Regular bra straps show through silk robes and qipao necklines</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Skin-colored bike shorts</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs text-stone-500">Modesty under Hanfu skirts + high-slit qipao</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Slip-on shoes</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs text-stone-500">Costume changes require shoe removal. Slip-ons save time.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Thin thermal layer (winter)</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs text-stone-500">Uniqlo Heattech under Hanfu, invisible under robes</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2.5 pr-4">No jewelry</td><td class="py-2.5 text-xs text-stone-500">Hanfu comes with its own accessories. Yours will clash.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">Photoshoot & Electronics</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">Reference photos on phone. Light base makeup applied before arriving. Portable charger 20,000 mAh minimum. Small mirror for pose checks. If booking photographer: ask for unedited RAW files too.</p>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">Weather-Specific Extras</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-stone-900">Spring (March–May)</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1">Light jacket, folding umbrella (frequent drizzle), allergy meds if you react to pollen. Best light for photos — golden hour around 5:30-6:30 PM in most cities.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-stone-900">Summer (June–August)</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1">Sunscreen SPF50+, wide-brim hat, sweat-proof makeup setting spray, cooling wipes, electrolyte tablets. Silk Hanfu is lightest for heat; avoid heavy brocade Tang suits. Change shirts if you sweat through.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-stone-900">Autumn (September–November)</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1">Layers that can be removed for photos. Beijing and Xi''an can drop 15\u00b0C between day and night. A packable down vest under Hanfu is invisible and warm.</p></div>
      <div class="bg-stone-50 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-stone-900">Winter (December–February)</h3><p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-1">Full Uniqlo Heattech set (top/bottom/socks), insulated gloves with touchscreen fingertips, hand warmers (sold at every convenience store in China). Snow on ancient city walls creates stunning photos — worth braving the cold.</p></div>
    </div>
    <h2 class="font-serif-sc text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-14 mb-4">What NOT to Bring</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-600">
      <li><strong>Excessive toiletries:</strong> Watsons, Miniso, and convenience stores are everywhere. Shampoo, toothpaste, and sunscreen are cheaper locally.</li>
      <li><strong>Heavy guidebooks:</strong> Use your phone — download maps and translation offline via Google Maps (works with VPN) or Maps.me.</li>
      <li><strong>Dress shoes:</strong> You''ll walk 15,000-25,000 steps/day at ancient sites. Comfortable walking shoes are non-negotiable.</li>
      <li><strong>Drone:</strong> Banned at most historical sites, city walls, and near military areas. Confiscation risk not worth it for casual travel photography.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="mt-8"><a href="/plan-trip" class="text-sm text-stone-400 hover:text-stone-600 transition-colors">Back to Plan Your Trip</a></div>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
